Q31) What is upcasting?
Answer: Child object stored in parent reference (automatic).
Example: Parent p = new Child();

Q32) What is downcasting?
Answer: Parent reference cast back to child type (explicit).
Example: Child c = (Child)p;

Q33) Predict:
Parent p = new Child();
p.childOnlyMethod();
A) Compile error
B) Runtime error
C) Works fine
D) Warning only
Correct Answer: A
Explanation: Compiler checks reference type methods.

Q34) Runtime trap:
--------------------------------
Parent p = new Parent();
Child c = (Child)p;
What happens?
A) Compile error
B) ClassCastException at runtime
C) Works fine
D) NullPointerException
Correct Answer: B
Explanation: Actual object is Parent, cannot be treated as Child.

Q35) Safe downcast check:
Answer: Use instanceof before casting.
Explanation: if(p instanceof Child) { Child c=(Child)p; }

